            <ArticleTitle>Is it always Alzheimer's? Let's talk to our patients about &quot;cardiocerebrovascular&quot; prevention.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>159-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s40520-015-0480-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Unlike Alzheimer's, vascular dementia can, in part, be prevented. The preventive approach foresees treatment for high blood pressure, atrial fibrillation, diabetes, high cholesterol, low HDL cholesterol, sedentary lifestyle, smoking, alcohol abuse, obesity, and sleep apnea. Moreover, also a well-balanced diet and physical activity are cornerstones of prevention, with beneficial effects on the brain and cognition.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
